                    "Use the MyUPMC app. After you log in, select Appointments, then pick a date and time that fits your schedule. This is applicable for UPMC providers only.",
                    "App: Go to Account, then Preferences.",
                    "Member site: select Profile Settings, then scroll down to Communication Preferences",
                    "Once you register for an account and log in, you can:\r\nCommunicate with your UPMC providers.\r\nSchedule and manage in-person and virtual appointments.\r\nView your medical record, providers' notes, and test results.\r\nRenew your prescriptions.\r\nPay bills you received from UPMC providers.",
                    "Visit MyUPMC.com to access your account or download the MyUPMC app from the or",
                    "Need help with UPMC Health Plan's digital tools? We can help! Contact our specialized Tech Guide team of experts at 1-833-685-5418 (TTY: 711) Monday through Friday from 8 a.m. to 5 p.m.",
                    "Communicate with your UPMC providers.",
                    "Schedule and manage in-person and virtual appointments.",
                    "View your medical record, providers' notes, and test results.",
                    "Renew your prescriptions.",
                    "Pay bills you received from UPMC providers.",
                    "Before you seek care from providers, we recommend that you review your plan documents. You can find them by going to Coverage Overview on the UPMC Health Plan member site or logging into the UPMC Health Plan app.\r\n\r\nYou will see a grid that outlines some of your most commonly used benefits, copayments for different types of providers, your coinsurance, and your deductible (if applicable).\r\n\r\nFor detailed information about your plan, see your Schedule of Benefits. This document:\r\nExplains your copayment, deductible, and coinsurance amounts, as well as your out-of-pocket maximum.\r\nLists health care services and their level of coverage.",
                    "Preventive care and screenings can help you stay healthy, reduce your risk of developing diseases, and keep conditions you have from becoming worse. All this may reduce your future health care expenses.",
                    "Getting the right preventive care can help you stay healthy, reduce your risk of developing diseases, and keep conditions you have from becoming worse. UPMC Health Plan covers many preventive care visits, screenings, and vaccines at no cost for members of all ages. This means you won’t have to pay anything. However, if your visit becomes diagnostic in nature—that is, if at your no-cost physical, your provider also hears a cough, and this results in a bronchitis diagnosis—you will be billed for the bronchitis diagnosis portion of the visit.\r\n\r\nCheck our list of preventive services and guidelines.",
                    "Explains your copayment, deductible, and coinsurance amounts, as well as your out-of-pocket maximum.",
                    "Lists health care services and their level of coverage.",
                    "Cost sharing is where you and UPMC Health Plan share the cost of your care. This means you must pay a portion of your health care expenses and UPMC Health Plan will pay a portion.\r\n\r\nYou have to pay your deductible before UPMC Health Plan will start covering your care costs. This means you'll pay for each covered service until you reach your deductible amount.\r\n\r\nThe Advantage Gold and Silver plans include copayments for certain medical services. Typically, you pay copayments at the time you receive a service (your deductible and coinsurance typically do not apply to services with a copayment).\r\n\r\nCoinsurance is your share of the cost of covered services after you meet your deductible. UPMC Health Plan will pay the rest. You'll pay your share until you meet your out-of-pocket maximum. If your coinsurance is 20 percent, you must pay 20 percent of the cost of covered health care services. UPMC Health Plan will pay the remaining 80 percent.\r\n\r\nYou will keep paying your share of the cost of covered services you receive from in-network providers until you meet your out-of-pocket maximum. This is the most you will have to pay for covered health care expenses in a plan year. If you meet your out-of-pocket maximum, UPMC Health Plan will pay for 100 percent of your covered care for the remainder of the plan year.\r\n\r\nYou can view all of your plan's cost of care by going to Coverage Overview.",
                    "This card provides important information about your plan and your coverage.",
                    "Doctors may ask for this information to ensure that they participate in your network.\r\nYou’ll need this number to complete medical forms.\r\nThese are your cost-sharing amounts. They vary by service type.\r\nYou will receive your UPMC Health Plan member ID card in the mail. To view your digital member ID card, you can:",
                    "Go to the UPMC Health Plan member site home screen > Quick Links > Print or order an ID card",
                    "Download the free UPMC Health Plan app > Sign in > under the Insurance tab, navigate to ID Card",
                    "LifeSolutions® offers counseling sessions to help you address work or personal concerns. This can help you become healthier, happier, and more productive. You and members of your household are eligible to use LifeSolutions' valuable resources. Through this resource, you can access:\r\nUp to six no-cost, confidential coaching and counseling sessions for various issues, including emotional challenges, stress, depression, relationships, and work-related concerns. Sessions can be held virtually, in person, over the phone, or via text message or chat (available to members who are 14 years or older).\r\nNo-cost consultations related to financial wellness or legal issues.\r\nReferrals to community resources.\r\nAccess to an interactive website that contains professional and personal development resources.\r\nVisit lifesolutionsforyou.com today or call at 1-800-647-3327 (TTY: 711). Phones are answered 24/7/365. All services are private and confidential.\r\nLearn more about Lifesolutions",
                    "Up to six no-cost, confidential coaching and counseling sessions for various issues, including emotional challenges, stress, depression, relationships, and work-related concerns. Sessions can be held virtually, in person, over the phone, or via text message or chat (available to members who are 14 years or older).",
