                    "No matter your stage in life, you have access to exceptional services and programs.",
                    "You can go to a PCP or ob-gyn for preventive gynecological care. You do not need a referral. Select an obstetrician or gynecologist.",
                    "You can go to your participating ob-gyn for all covered obstetrical and gynecological care, including outpatient services and inpatient admissions. You should choose a gynecologist as soon as you become a UPMC Health Plan member so that he or she can help you stay healthy.",
                    "Your preventive care benefits may include the following:\r\nBreast cancer screenings (mammograms)\r\nCervical cancer screenings\r\nChlamydia screenings\r\nBone density screenings",
                    "UPMC medical plans include a fertility benefit with a $5,000 lifetime benefit maximum (medical and pharmacy combined). Covered members must receive care through a UPMC Health Plan participating provider who is a credentialed reproductive endocrinologist. If services are received at UPMC Magee-Womens Hospital (including satellite locations), an additional $2,000 discount is provided by UPMC Magee upon benefit exhaustion. Artificial insemination procedures including intracervical, intrauterine, and sperm washing for artificial insemination are not subject to the fertility benefit maximum and has no lifetime benefit limit.",
                    "With Baby Steps, UPMC Health Plan’s maternity program, you have access to maternity health coaches throughout your pregnancy and in the first few months after you give birth. If you have fertility or preconception questions, you can also get support through the program.\r\n\r\nThis program is designed as a supplement to the support that you receive from your ob-gyn. It can also help optimize your health and wellness before, during, and after pregnancy.\r\n\r\nYou can connect with a maternity health coach virtually through the UPMC Health Plan member site.",
                    "Our coaches are registered nurses with a background in obstetrics. They often talk to members about these and other topics:\r\nMedications that are safe to take while pregnant\r\nSigns of complications and when to call a doctor\r\nPain relief options during labor\r\nBaby care basics\r\nThe benefits of breast-feeding and how to continue after returning to work\r\n\r\nTo talk with a maternity health coach, call 1-866-778-6073 (TTY: 711), send an email to Maternitycoaches@upmc.edu to schedule a phone call, or live chat with a health coach using the chat function on the UPMC Health Plan member site or app. Coaches are available Monday through Friday from 7 a.m. to 8 p.m. EST and Saturday from 8 a.m. to 3 p.m. EST.",
                    "Your UPMC Health Plan coverage includes breastfeeding classes. Additionally, if you intend to breastfeed after giving birth, you can receive a breast pump (valued at more than $200) at no cost.\r\n\r\nYou may obtain a breast pump if you have not received one from UPMC Health Plan within the past three years, or if your pump is broken or out of warranty.",
