                    "UPMC Health Plan is committed to helping you strengthen or maintain your mental health. That’s why our care management includes support for emotional and mental wellness. This includes:\r\nSubstance use.\r\nBereavement issues.\r\nMarital or family concerns.\r\nHealth coaching support.\r\nAs a UPMC Health Plan member, you also have access to our behavioral health programs to overcome anxiety, stress, or depression. You can access these programs—free of charge—through our behavioral health coaches. They are licensed professionals with behavioral health training, and ready to help you determine the most effective ways to address your behavioral health needs.\r\nYou can find a provider or treatment center by visiting our provider directory and selecting Behavioral Health as the kind of care you're seeking. Be sure to check on whether your provider is in your network\r\n\r\nYou can also call UPMC Health Plan Behavioral Health Services at 1-888-251-0083. (TTY: 711) Our behavioral health team is available Monday through Friday from 8 a.m. to 5 p.m.\r\nPodcast: Digital Tools for Your Mental Health\r\nLaura Francis, director of Behavioral Health Clinical Programs at UPMC Health Plan takes a Health Break to discuss how free digital tools for our members can support mental health and well-being.\r\nHealth Break: Digital tools for your mental health | UPMC MyHealth Matters",
                    "Substance use.\r\nBereavement issues.\r\nMarital or family concerns.\r\nHealth coaching support.",
                    "As a UPMC Health Plan member, you also have access to our behavioral health programs to overcome anxiety, stress, or depression. You can access these programs—free of charge—through our behavioral health coaches. They are licensed professionals with behavioral health training, and ready to help you determine the most effective ways to address your behavioral health needs.",
                    "You can find a provider or treatment center by visiting our provider directory and selecting Behavioral Health as the kind of care you're seeking. Be sure to check on whether your provider is in your network\r\n\r\nYou can also call UPMC Health Plan Behavioral Health Services at 1-888-251-0083. (TTY: 711) Our behavioral health team is available Monday through Friday from 8 a.m. to 5 p.m.",
                    "If you or a family member experiences an emergency, please call 911 or your local ambulance service, call or text 988 for the Suicide and Crisis Lifeline (available nationwide), or go to the nearest emergency room. After you are discharged, contact your PCP as soon as possible to schedule follow-up care.\r\n\r\nA health coach can connect you with a mental health professional to make sure you get support when you need it. If your health coach determines that you are in danger or may harm yourself, he or she will act quickly to get you emergency help. Your health coach can:\r\nRefer you to an emergency department.\r\nDispatch a mobile crisis team.\r\nHelp you get an appointment within 24 hours.\r\n\r\nIf you are in crisis, please call 911, call or text 988 for the Suicide & Crisis Lifeline (available anywhere as a national resource), go to the nearest emergency room, or call the local ambulance service.",
